---
id: RL-006
type: rule
family: responsibility-laundering
title: Reply disguised as fix
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 6

targets: [agent-output, pr-description]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: (reply\s+only|acknowledged|noted)\s*[|│].*\b(addressed|fixed|resolved)\b
  flags: i

related: []
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Summary tables should distinguish between actual fixes and
acknowledgments. Counting a "reply only" or "noted" item as "addressed"
or "fixed" inflates the work done and hides unresolved items.

Separate reply-only items from fixes in summaries. If an item was
acknowledged but not changed, label it honestly — "acknowledged, no
action taken" or "replied, user to decide."
